  "attributionNote": "The discourse is presented in the canonical collection as the Buddha's teaching, transmitted by the early Buddhist community. Authorship of the surviving Pali text is collective and anonymous.",
  "description": "The Shorter Discourse at Gosiṅga is sutta 31 of the Majjhima Nikāya (Middle Length Discourses). The Middle Length Discourses gather 152 suttas of the Pali canon, among them the Satipaṭṭhāna, the Alagaddūpama and the Cūḷamālukya suttas. They are preserved in Pali and translated here by Bhikkhu Sujato.",
